hwmon: (ina2xx) fix INA234 power register scaling (16x too high)

INA234 is a 12-bit part. The driver scales current_lsb up by
2^current_shift and shifts the current/shunt/bus registers back down on
read, but the power register is read unshifted. power_lsb therefore keeps
the extra 2^current_shift factor, so power*_input reads 16x too high on
INA234 while current and the voltages read correctly.

Remove the factor from power_lsb in ina2xx_set_shunt(). current_shift is 0
for the 16-bit parts (INA219/226/260), so they are unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@zaman.io>
---
--- a/drivers/hwmon/ina2xx.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/ina2xx.c
@@ -881,8 +881,16 @@ static int ina2xx_set_shunt(struct ina2x
 
 	data->rshunt = val;
 	data->current_lsb_uA = DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(dividend, val);
-	data->power_lsb_uW = data->config->power_lsb_factor *
-			     data->current_lsb_uA;
+	/*
+	 * For 12-bit parts (INA234) current_lsb is scaled up by
+	 * 2^current_shift and the current/voltage registers are shifted back
+	 * down on read; the power register is read unshifted, so the same
+	 * factor has to be removed from power_lsb here or power reads
+	 * 2^current_shift too high (16x on INA234). current_shift is 0 for the
+	 * 16-bit parts, so they are unaffected.
+	 */
+	data->power_lsb_uW = (data->config->power_lsb_factor *
+			      data->current_lsb_uA) >> data->config->current_shift;
 
 	return 0;
 }
